It is amazing that you actually climbed up this high!	你居然爬到這麼高的地方，真是令人驚訝！
It is hard to believe those seeds you planted grew this high.	真難以置信，你種下的種子居然長得這麼高。
You are in the Land of the Clouds.  It is rumored a giant lives up here.	你身處雲之國，傳說有個巨人住在這上面。
While falling through the hole, the magic ring fell off your finger.  Dangerous creatures can see you now!	你掉落洞穴的途中，魔戒從你的手指上滑落了。危險的生物現在能看見你了！
The warm sunlight falls through the hole in the ceiling.  Unfortunately, you can't reach it.	溫暖的陽光從天花板的洞口灑落下來，可惜你搆不著。
The dark tunnel leads off to the south.	這條黑暗的隧道通往南方。
When you fell through the hole, you felt a streching sensation and are back to your normal size.	你掉落洞穴時感到一陣拉伸的感覺，恢復成原本的大小了。
The further you get from the light, the darker and mustier it becomes.	你離光源越遠，這裡就變得越昏暗、越潮濕發霉。
Being invisible won't hide you from this rat's keen sense of smell.	就算隱形，也躲不過這隻大老鼠敏銳的嗅覺。
There is no rat here.	這裡沒有大老鼠。
It is a big rat with dripping teeth and small, greedy eyes.	這是一隻大老鼠，牙齒滴著口水，眼睛小而貪婪。
It is very dark and dreary.  The rat seems to like it here.	這裡又暗又陰森，那隻大老鼠似乎很喜歡待在這裡。
It is very dark and dreary in here.	這裡又暗又陰森。
This is no mouse, this is a big, ugly rat!	這可不是老鼠，這是一隻又大又醜的大老鼠！
The door slowly opens.	門緩緩打開了。
The door is closed.	門已經關上了。
Be careful around this rat next time!  He's dangerous!!	下次小心那隻大老鼠！牠很危險！！
The door appears to be stuck and won't close.	這扇門似乎卡住了，關不上。
Get closer if you want to try.	想試試看的話，先靠近一點。
You can't.  He moves too quickly.	你辦不到，牠的動作太快了。
The rat rasps, "Treasure!  Treasure!  Give treasure, or no go door!  Give treasure NOW!"	大老鼠沙啞地說：「寶物！寶物！交出寶物，不然別想過門！現在就交出寶物！」
You have no treasure to give the rat.	你身上沒有寶物可以給那隻大老鼠。
The rat doesn't want an ordinary walnut.	大老鼠不想要一顆普通的胡桃。
The rat doesn't want a tattered pouch.	大老鼠不想要一個破爛的皮袋。
What kind of treasure would you like to give the  greedy rat?	你想給這隻貪心的大老鼠什麼樣的寶物？
The huge rat takes the treasure you have offered and scuttles away.	那隻巨大的老鼠接過你獻上的寶物，飛快地跑走了。
It appears you are afraid of the rat!  You must get closer to give anything to this rat!	看來你很怕那隻大老鼠！你得靠近一點，才能把東西交給牠！
You do not have any.	你身上沒有這東西。
The rat drools at the sight of the cheese... and snatches it from your hand.  You might want to count your fingers.	大老鼠一看到乳酪就流口水……一把從你手中搶走。你也許該數數自己的手指還在不在。
The rat scrambles to the wall and seems to magically merge with it.	大老鼠竄向牆壁，彷彿被魔法融進牆裡消失了。
That is a good idea, but you do not have any cheese.	這主意不錯，可惜你身上沒有乳酪。
You count your fingers and are relieved to see you still have all of them.	你數了數自己的手指，鬆了口氣，發現十根都還在。
The leprechauns' magic powers detect your unseen presence.	地穴人的魔法察覺到你隱形的存在。
The leprechauns do not like your invasion of their territory.  They may not let you get any further.	地穴人不喜歡你入侵他們的地盤，他們可能不會讓你再往前一步。
The leprechauns revere the power of the fourleaf clover. With it in your possession they will leave you absolutely alone.	地穴人敬畏幸運草的力量，只要你身上帶著它，他們就絕對不會來打擾你。
Leprechauns love fiddle music!  Have you ever seen such frenzied dancing?	地穴人最愛小提琴的音樂！你看過這麼瘋狂的舞蹈嗎？
Totally involved in the music, they dance right out of the room.	他們完全沉浸在音樂裡，一路跳著舞離開了房間。
The leprechaun catches you and holds you with his small,  but strong arms.  I don't think the leprechaun will ever let go.	地穴人抓住了你，用他矮小卻強壯的雙臂緊緊抱住你。我想他大概永遠不會放手了。
You are in the antechamber of the Hall of the Leprechaun King.  There are leprechauns in the room with you.	你身處地穴人國王大廳的前廳，房間裡還有其他地穴人。
I can think of no good reason to close the door.	我實在想不出關門的理由。
I would not try talking to the leprechauns.  You might say the wrong thing.	我勸你別跟地穴人搭話，你可能會說錯話。
You would not get all of them before they got you.	你還沒抓到他們全部，他們就先抓住你了。
There are not any leprechauns here.	這裡沒有地穴人。
You are already playing the fiddle.	你已經在拉小提琴了。
You find playing the fiddle here very fun, but the dance floor is in the other room.	在這裡拉小提琴挺有趣的，不過舞池在隔壁房間。
You play a little tune on the fiddle to amuse yourself.	你拉了一小段曲子自娛自樂。
It is very difficult to play a fiddle if you do not have one.	沒有小提琴，很難拉得出曲子。
The little green men do not seem to be noticing you; perhaps because of the fourleaf clover.	這些綠色小人似乎沒注意到你，也許是幸運草的緣故。
There aren't any leprechauns here.	這裡沒有地穴人。
The King of the leprechauns is sitting on the stone throne. The magic shield is next to the throne.	地穴人國王坐在石造王座上，靈盾就放在王座旁邊。
The King of the leprechauns is sitting on the stone throne.	地穴人國王坐在石造王座上。
The King is leaving.	國王正要離開。
The King of the leprechauns is no longer here.	地穴人國王已經不在這裡了。
The stairs go up a narrow tunnel.	階梯通往一條狹窄的隧道。
To see the stairs, you have to get closer.	你得靠近一點，才能看清楚那道階梯。
The leprechaun King ignores your words.	地穴人國王對你的話置之不理。
I hope you can escape from the leprechauns, but it doesn't look good for you.	希望你能逃過地穴人的手掌心，不過看來情況對你不太妙。
The leprechaun, with much support from his peers, catches you and refuses to let go.  I think you will be here for a long, long time.	那個地穴人在同伴的協助下抓住了你，說什麼也不肯放手。我看你要在這裡待上好長一段時間了。
The King's magic prevents you from getting close enough to harm him.	國王的魔法讓你無法靠近到能傷害他的距離。
After his followers have danced away, the King of the leprechauns realizes he can lead best by following, and leaves, forgetting his beautiful sceptre.	隨著臣民跳舞遠去，地穴人國王領悟到，跟隨才是最好的領導方式，於是也跟著離去，忘了帶走他美麗的王杖。
The shield is already in your pocket.	靈盾已經在你的口袋裡了。
I think there might have been a shield here once, but someone has since taken it.	我想這裡原本可能有面盾牌，但已經被人拿走了。
The shield is no longer here.	這裡已經沒有盾牌了。
It is made of titanium and is rimmed with jewels.	靈盾以鈦金屬打造，邊緣鑲著珠寶。
As inconspicuously as possible, you add the shield to what you are carrying.	你不動聲色地把靈盾收進了行囊。
You take the magic shield and carefully put it in your pocket.	你拿起靈盾，小心翼翼地放進口袋。
You need to get closer to see it clearly.	你得靠近一點才能看清楚。
You must be closer to do that.	你得靠近一點才能這麼做。
I see no sceptre right here.	這裡沒看到什麼王杖。
I see no sceptre to get around here.	這附近沒看到可以拿的王杖。
Eagerly, you pick up the sceptre.	你迫不及待地拾起了王杖。
I see no sceptre in the vicinity.	這附近沒看到王杖。
There is no sceptre in sight to get.	視線範圍內沒有可拿的王杖。
The leprechauns seem irritated by your invasion of their territory.  I would be real careful about what I say and do right now!	地穴人似乎對你入侵他們的地盤感到惱怒。我勸你現在言行都得格外小心！
This is the throne room of the leprechaun King.	這裡是地穴人國王的王座廳。
This is the throne room of the leprechaun King.  There is a shield and a sceptre near the throne.	這裡是地穴人國王的王座廳，王座附近有一面盾牌和一根王杖。
This is the throne room of the leprechaun King.  There is a shield next to the throne.	這裡是地穴人國王的王座廳，王座旁邊有一面盾牌。
This is the throne room of the leprechaun King.  There is a sceptre next to the throne.	這裡是地穴人國王的王座廳，王座旁邊有一根王杖。
The stairs are very steep and narrow.	這道階梯又陡又窄。
This is a small cave with stairs on one side and a very small hole on the other side.	這是一個小洞穴，一側有階梯，另一側有個非常小的洞。
You seem to be stuck in these underground caverns.  As you have no way of leaving, it looks like you'll spend the rest of your life here.	你似乎被困在這片地底洞穴裡。既然沒有辦法離開，看來你得在這裡度過餘生了。
You dare not jump here or you would go through the floor!	你可不敢在這裡跳，不然會直接摔穿地板！
The cottage is run-down and sparsely furnished.  The only nice possession seems to be a fiddle in the corner.	這間小屋破舊不堪，家具寥寥無幾，唯一像樣的東西似乎是角落那把小提琴。
The cottage is run-down and sparsely furnished.	這間小屋破舊不堪，家具寥寥無幾。
This family is so poor, they can't even repair the floor.	這戶人家窮到連地板都修不起。
This is the woodcutter's fiddle.	這是樵夫的小提琴。
The woodcutter is thin and dressed in rags.	樵夫瘦骨嶙峋，衣衫襤褸。
The woodcutter's wife is skinny and poorly dressed.	樵夫的妻子骨瘦如柴，衣著寒酸。
The woodcutter and his wife are sitting at the old oak table.	樵夫和他的妻子坐在那張老橡木桌旁。
"Welcome to my humble abode."	「歡迎來到寒舍。」
She replies, "I'd like to offer you something, but we do not even have food for ourselves."	她回答道：「我很想招待你，可是我們連自己的食物都不夠了。」
"Make yourself at home in our humble home."	「請把這寒舍當自己家吧。」
That would be very nice.  How do you want to help them?	這真是個好主意，你想怎麼幫助他們呢？
What an abominable idea!  You should be ashamed of yourself for even suggesting such a thing!	這主意真是可惡！你居然想得出這種點子，該感到羞愧！
It is closed, but in this house, all the cabinets are bare.	櫃子關著，不過在這戶人家裡，所有的櫥櫃都是空的。
The cabinet is all but bare.	這個櫥櫃幾乎是空的。
The beautiful scenery outside is in contrast to the dreariness inside.	屋外的美麗景色，和屋內的淒涼景象形成強烈對比。
You should have more sympathy for these poor folks!	你應該多同情一下這些可憐人！
You have given the bowl to these poor people and it is now theirs.  You have no right to take it back.	你已經把碗送給這對可憐的夫妻了，它現在是他們的東西，你沒有權利拿回來。
The woodcutters admire the bowl as it sits on their table.	樵夫夫妻欣賞著放在桌上的那只碗。
What treasure do you wish to donate to them?	你想捐贈什麼寶物給他們？
The woodcutter and his wife very gratefully accept the treasure.  "This will help us for awhile," says the woodcutter.	樵夫和他的妻子滿懷感激地收下了寶物。樵夫說：「這能幫我們撐一陣子了。」
This is a nice thought, but unfortunately you have nothing to give these poor people.	這番心意很好，可惜你身上沒有東西能給這對可憐的夫妻。
The woodcutter and his wife kindly accept your gift of food.  They offer a heartfelt "Thank you."	樵夫和他的妻子親切地收下了你贈送的食物，由衷地向你道謝。
Puzzled, the couple wonders why you have given them a bowl.	這對夫妻一頭霧水，不明白你為什麼給他們一只碗。
The woodcutter family is very grateful that you have given them a bowl of stew.  Now they will have at least one last meal.  As a token of their gratitude, they offer their last earthly possession, the woodcutter's fiddle.	樵夫一家對你送上的這碗燉肉萬分感激，這下他們至少能吃上最後一餐了。為了表達謝意，他們獻上了僅剩的財產——樵夫的那把小提琴。
Eat stew from an empty bowl?  The woodcutters are beginning to question your authenticity.	從空碗裡吃燉肉？樵夫夫妻開始懷疑你是不是有問題。
The stew looks delicious, but it is no longer yours.  Now you will have to do without.	這碗燉肉看起來很美味，可惜已經不是你的了，你現在只能餓著了。
The couple is amazed and delighted as the bowl miraculously fills with a bubbling stew.  As a token of their gratitude, they offer their last earthly possession, the woodcutter's fiddle.	這對夫妻又驚又喜，眼看著碗裡奇蹟般地冒出滾燙的燉肉。為了表達謝意，他們獻上了僅剩的財產——樵夫的那把小提琴。
The couple does not understand.	這對夫妻聽不懂。
The fiddle is a beautiful instrument made of polished wood.	這把小提琴是用打磨光亮的木材製成的精美樂器。
You cannot take their last precious possession!	你不能拿走他們僅剩的珍貴財產！
The polished wood feels like satin -- it seems to still vibrate from the last song it played.	打磨過的木頭摸起來像緞子一樣光滑——彷彿還殘留著上一首曲子的餘韻在震動。
What a terrible suggestion!  These people are poor and starving and you want to steal one of their last earthly possessions.	這主意真是糟透了！這些人又窮又餓，你居然想偷走他們僅剩的財產之一。
You cannot see it very well from here.	從這裡看不太清楚。
I doubt that you will get away with it, but you will have to get closer to try.	我不認為你能得逞，不過你得先靠近一點才能試試看。
These poor people can't even afford to repair the floor!  Sorry about that.	這對可憐的夫妻連地板都修不起！抱歉了。
As soon as you entered the house the old goat ran away.	你一走進屋子，那隻老山羊就跑掉了。
"Hello"	「哈囉」
There is an empty bowl sitting on the old oak table.	那張老橡木桌上放著一只空碗。
There is a bowl of stew sitting on the old oak table.	那張老橡木桌上放著一碗燉肉。
The view is magnificent.	這景色壯麗極了。
Now is not the time to irritate the witch.	現在可不是惹惱巫婆的時候。
Now is not a good time to bother the bird.	現在不是打擾那隻鳥的好時機。
